config tui needs an option for setting serverity of unused/uncalled/etc functions/vars/etc. They should be info by default, not warning. In normal cli check run, we don't want to spam the log with lots of unused stuff. The info msgs should be hidden by default (showing only a summary) and then a cli flag lets you see them. This might not gel perfectly with existing design, so discuss with Max the new design first to make sure we get it working well, smoothyl, etc, and so it works well for me by default.


---

## Design decisions (Max + agent session, 2026-08-31)

Assessment: ~60% pre-existing. UnusedLevel (ignore|hint|info|warn|error) +
aliases, --unused/--no-unused, workspace/user config, and the config-TUI
`unused` entry (user_config.rs SETTINGS) all exist; info/hint already never
fail the run even under --warnings-as-errors.

Remaining work + approved decisions:

1. Default flip `UnusedLevel::Warn` -> `Info` (config.rs default; help,
   README, CHANGELOG; test fallout).
2. Fold **by severity, not by family**: one-shot plain/pretty output hides
   ALL INFO and HINT diagnostics by default, whatever produced them.
3. Reveal flag: `--show-info`. No config key for it (per-run choice).
4. Trailer/summary: never claim "0 diagnostics" when items are hidden.
   Shape: `1 error, 2 warnings in <root> (14 info hidden — --show-info to
   list)`; with nothing visible: `0 errors/warnings (14 info hidden)`.
   ADDITION (Max): the summary also shows counts of the various KINDS
   within the severities that were generated (e.g. per-kind breakdown of
   the hidden infos).
5. Scope: one-shot CLI human output only. JSON stays complete (machine
   contract), LSP server keeps publishing everything (editors render
   info/hint faded natively), watch TUI untouched (its display lives
   under GH #8).
6. `hint` folds along with `info`.
7. Single family-wide knob stays; per-kind severities are YAGNI
   (unused_callbacks exemption list already covers "intentional").

Known behavior change: CI lanes using --warnings-as-errors stop failing on
unused once the default is info; --unused warn|error is the opt-back-in.
Implementation in worktree .worktrees/b090.